  "executive_briefing": "As of late August 2026, the digital asset sector is defined by a transition toward institutional consolidation and regulatory maturation. The U.S. legislative landscape is dominated by the Digital Asset Market Clarity Act (H.R. 3633), which serves as the primary pivot point for establishing federal market structure. Institutional adoption of Bitcoin ETFs has shifted from speculative growth to a normalized, albeit slower, integration phase. Simultaneously, the technical rivalry between the EVM-based DeFi ecosystem and Bitcoin-native execution layers\u2014specifically those utilizing the Clarity language for deterministic security\u2014has emerged as a focal point for institutional developers seeking to mitigate reentrancy risks. Decentralized cross-chain liquidity remains an active development area, prioritizing native asset movement over insecure, wrapped-token bridges.",
